## The Numbers Don't Lie

In the year 2026, we've already seen 337 food recalls, 91 of which were Class I, posing severe health risks. A disheartening number of these are repeat offenders, with 68 brands showing up more than once. 

## The Bright Yellow Flag

This past week, recalls for unapproved food colorings dominated the headlines. Guangdong Zonegoing Food Co., LTD, responsible for the 52USA brand Popping Boba, had multiple products flagged. These recalls cited the inclusion of tartrazine (Yellow 5), sunset yellow (Yellow 6), and allura red (Red 40)--colors either unapproved or undeclared.

### Brand Breakdown

Top offenders include Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC, each racking up double-digit recalls--all Class I.

## What You Can Do

1. Review product labels for known allergen triggers.
2. Avoid products from repeat offenders until clear improvement is demonstrated.

## Conclusion

This spate of recalls reinforces the critical need for transparency and accountability in food production. Be a proactive consumer.
